.TH RANGE 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Value Types"
.SH NAME
range \- built-in range value type methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ranges in y-- represent a mathematical sequence of numbers from a start to an end
with a specified step. They are evaluated lazily but can be converted to lists.
.SH METHODS
.TP
\fBmin()\fR -> int()|float()
Returns the minimum value achievable within the range bounds.
.TP
\fBmax()\fR -> int()|float()
Returns the maximum value achievable within the range bounds.
.TP
\fBstep()\fR -> int()|float()
Returns the step size of the range.
.TP
\fBreverse([modify_original=true])\fR -> range()
Reverses the direction of the range. For example, a range from 1 to 10 with step 1
becomes 10 to 1 with step -1.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
list(3)
